WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:06.000 line:18% position:40% size:74% align:center
A narrow valley. A changing direction.
All three methods start together.

00:06.000 --> 00:16.000 line:18% position:40% size:74% align:center
GD follows the current slope.
Momentum also carries the previous motion.

00:16.000 --> 00:27.000 line:18% position:40% size:74% align:center
Adam remembers gradients and their squared sizes.
It adjusts the step separately for each coordinate.

00:27.000 --> 00:40.000 line:18% position:40% size:74% align:center
Watch the turn, not just the finish.
The same valley produces different paths.

00:40.000 --> 00:48.000 line:18% position:40% size:74% align:center
An adaptive step is not always a shortcut.
Compare the two graphs below.
